ritical issue in transmon-based quantum computing by suppressing unwanted state transitions in qubit readout.\n\nRead the Letter: https://t.co/ZT7A3eoWwC https://t.co/eIda1gN8HP", "url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2116214555613200845"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:57:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116212996188123323"], "id": "2116212996188123323", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 47, "impression_count": 77386, "like_count": 575, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 76, "retweet_count": 29}, "text": "Either because people won’t let themselves believe the polls or because people don’t have the bandwidth to contemplate novel developments. But nobody’s really talking about the possibility that by next week, Texas, Kansas, Iowa, and Ohio are Blue states and what that really means", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116212996188123323"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:57:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116212895143149820"], "id": "2116212895143149820", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2130, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "I've been a fan of @paulfain , @elyseashburn and Work/Shift for a long time... and I finally got to chat to Paul live a few weeks ago.\n\nThe topics: AI, the labor market and @GuildEducation 's perspective on both.  Watch:\n\nhttps://t.co/1J5dIhgri9", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116212895143149820"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:42:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116209082785026123"], "id": "2116209082785026123", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 33, "impression_count": 86123, "like_count": 1211, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 66, "retweet_count": 27}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115906304308838419", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Good. People with children should pay less. I’ve contributed to the future of the species. Now give me my 